   "source": [
    "# Phase 3: UNSW-NB15 Cloud Security Preprocessing & Pipeline Export\n",
    "## Project: Adaptive Learning for Cloud Security and Predictive Maintenance\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    "Transform raw UNSW-NB15 dataset files (`UNSW_NB15_training-set.csv` and `UNSW_NB15_testing-set.csv`) into clean, standardized, model-ready formats. The notebook imports the reusable logic from `src/data_processing/security_preprocessing.py` to ensure **zero data leakage** and exports the fitted pipeline object to `models/security/preprocessing_pipeline.joblib`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure path to src is available\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))) if '__file__' in locals() else os.path.abspath('..')\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, 'src'))\n",
    "\n",
    "from data_processing.security_preprocessing import preprocess_unsw_nb15\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Module import successful!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 1. Rationale for Preprocessing Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "### A. Column Dropping (`id`):\n",
    "- The `id` column is a sequential transaction index (1, 2, 3...). It carries zero network domain intelligence. Leaving `id` in the dataset would introduce spurious correlations and risk trivial data leakage. Therefore, `id` is explicitly dropped.\n",
    "\n",
    "### B. Categorical Feature Encoding (`OneHotEncoder`):\n",
    "- Categorical columns (`proto`, `service`, `state`) are nominal with no natural rank or numerical order. `OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', sparse_output=False)` is used to convert nominal categories into independent binary indicator variables. Label encoding is avoided for features because linear and distance-based models would misinterpret arbitrary numerical values (e.g. `tcp`=1, `udp`=2).\n",
    "\n",
    "### C. Numerical Feature Scaling (`StandardScaler`):\n",
    "- Continuous traffic features (`dur`, `sbytes`, `dbytes`, `sload`, `dload`, `rate`) exhibit widely varying scale magnitudes. `StandardScaler` standardizes features to zero mean ($\mu=0$) and unit variance ($\sigma=1$).\n",
    "\n",
    "### D. Zero Data Leakage Verification:\n",
    "- All transformers (`OneHotEncoder`, `StandardScaler`, `LabelEncoder`) are **fitted strictly on the training set (`X_train`)**. The fitted transformers are then applied to transform both `X_train` and `X_test`. `X_test` data is never observed during fitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 2. Execute Preprocessing Engine"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results = preprocess_unsw_nb15()\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train = results['X_train']\n",
    "X_test = results['X_test']\n",
    "y_train_binary = results['y_train_binary']\n",
    "y_test_binary = results['y_test_binary']\n",
    "y_train_multiclass = results['y_train_multiclass']\n",
    "y_test_multiclass = results['y_test_multiclass']\n",
    "pipeline_path = results['pipeline_path']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 3. Dataset Shape & Target Class Distribution Inspection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=== PROCESSED DATASET SHAPES ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"X_train shape               : {X_train.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"X_test shape                : {X_test.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"y_train_binary shape        : {y_train_binary.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"y_test_binary shape         : {y_test_binary.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"y_train_multiclass shape    : {y_train_multiclass.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"y_test_multiclass shape     : {y_test_multiclass.shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== BINARY TARGET DISTRIBUTION (TRAIN) ===\")\n",
    "print(pd.Series(y_train_binary).value_counts(normalize=True).map('{:.2%}'.format))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== MULTICLASS TARGET DISTRIBUTION (TRAIN) ===\")\n",
    "multiclass_counts = pd.Series(results['attack_cat_train_raw']).value_counts()\n",
    "multiclass_pcts = pd.Series(results['attack_cat_train_raw']).value_counts(normalize=True).map('{:.2%}'.format)\n",
    "df_multi_summary = pd.DataFrame({'Count': multiclass_counts, 'Percentage': multiclass_pcts})\n",
    "display(df_multi_summary)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSaved Pipeline Path: {pipeline_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 4. Phase 3 Checkpoint Verification\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Leakage-Free Guarantee**: Encoders and Scalers were fitted ONLY on `X_train` and transformed `X_test` using the saved pipeline object.\n",
    "2. **Target Preservation**: Original string attack categories (`attack_cat_raw`) are preserved in exported processed files for prediction output rendering.\n",
    "3. **Pipeline Artifact Export**: Pipeline artifact successfully written to `models/security/preprocessing_pipeline.joblib`."
   ]
  }
